WEBVTT

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.050
Nothing less from the son
of a traditional chef!

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.420
Mizoguchi Deluxe Fried Rice!

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.380
A Mizoguchi specialty?

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.050
That has an ominous ring to it.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.920
Mother says: "It is not how much we do,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.420
but how much love we put in the doing."

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.880
Though you've put a lot
of love into yourself!

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.170
You're quotin' Mother Teresa, right?

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.800
Doesn't take much to make her laugh.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.800
Ahem. Anyway...

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.210
Let's save our new members'
introductions for later,

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.510
and dig in!

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.880
Let's eat!

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.380
It's good!

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.090
Oh man, it's nice and crumbly!

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.460
I've never had fried rice
this tasty! Right?

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.010
Yeah!

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.460
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.510
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.300
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.130
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.420
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.670
<i>With that first step</i>

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.840
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.800
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.380
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.010
<i>just as you are</i>

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.170
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:05.670
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.300
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:12.170
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.420
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.550
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.760
I'm Tamotsu Kaneda, third-year.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.670
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.130
Someya, second-year, same.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.550
Norita, second-year, likewise.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.920
Your hair's gold, silver, and bronze,
so we'll call you Kin, Gin, and Doh.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.920
I see...

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.760
I think I get why you wanted to join.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.920
I'm Takeru Ando, a first-year!

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.420
Your team stood out the most at the
school festival, so I wanted to join, too!

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.460
We'll call you Outstanding Broccoli.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.300
Too long.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.170
Let's go with Takeru.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.920
Takuya Nabeshima, third-year.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.050
And I'm his little brother,
Takumi, a first-year!

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.460
We saw you onstage at the
school festival and thought...

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.550
You call yourselves the Breakers,
yet you don't do any breakdancing!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.590
Wait, what's so funny about that?

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.380
I think the two of you will make good bases.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.840
Weren't you watching us from the front row?

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.090
Yeah! I was! So you
noticed me. I'm so happy!

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.800
Uh, and your name?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.550
I'm Sakuma, a first-year!
So I'd like you to call me Saku.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:47.840
Whoa!

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.170
Wow.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.010
I was a ballerina as a kid!

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.340
Isn't that the word for a female ballet dancer?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.800
So, Saku, what's your first name?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.340
Ryuzo.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.090
"Dragon"?!

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.380
Okay, next!

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.260
Hisashi Mori, first-year.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.880
I came for Dreams' routine,
so I didn't see Breakers'.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.380
But the idea of an all-men's team...

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.880
...sounds so freaking impressive!

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.300
Even more than Yomei's team, Sparks!

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.760
Abso-freaking-lutely!

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.670
I knew this would be amazing.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.920
I look forward to the beginning of practice.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.840
Nice to meet you all!

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.880
And the last one is me.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.760
I'm Takagi, and starting today,
I'm the Breakers' full-time coach.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.340
I should've said this beforehand, but what you saw
at the school festival cannot be called cheerleading.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:56.710
The flyer was wobbly, and the bases and spotter
didn't fulfill their fundamental roles at all.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.460
They tossed and caught the flyer
with brute force alone,

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.670
essentially just throwing
him into the air.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.550
You guys are beyond bad.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.670
Beyond...

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.840
Bad...

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.510
So I've decided to become your coach.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.960
Any objections?

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.050
Yes?

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.130
Notta single one, Sis!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.840
Please call me Coach.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:30.220
<b>Caf</b>

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:30.220
<b>Sunflower</b>

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.550
Man, we got so many new members!

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.960
And so many strong personalities...

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.920
Kazu, did you know about Coach Takagi?

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.130
Nope. She just suddenly said she
wanted to come to today's meeting.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.550
To think she's gonna be
our full-time coach...

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.960
Sho.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.840
So here you are.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.130
Hashimoto.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.550
Uh, yes?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.260
Please add us to your message group, too.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:52.460
I will.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.920
Then I'm off.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.510
Haru, you heading to work?

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.210
Huh? Yeah.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.010
And so, Tokugawa here
will join us starting today.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.510
I look forward to working with you.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.300
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.050
Please take your time.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:20.010
Why're we working at the same place?

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.590
Because I lied earlier
about having a job here.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:25.050
But if I actually started working
it wouldn't be a lie anymore,

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.960
and having more members
will cost us more money...

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.050
Sho.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:30.920
What?

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:36.880
If you're unhappy that
Takagi's our coach now...

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:44.590
It's fine. We really need a proper coach so that
we don't get accused of just flinging people around.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.380
Yes, this is my son.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.130
He was supposed to start studyin'
second semester, but he was a tad late...

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.840
Nice t'meet you.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.550
Nice t'meet you...

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.510
S'gotta be fakin' that Kyoto dialect...

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:01.300
I'm hopin' you'll teach him some Japanese.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:05.510
Oh no, we're counting on him to
teach us Chinese! Right, Haru?

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:06.510
Huh?

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.920
Welp, I'll be off.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.050
Oh, that's one of our newbies.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.670
What's-his-name...

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:19.380
Oh, Hisashi!

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.920
Sir.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.260
Sir?

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.260
That's right, we're your superiors!

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.630
Ask us anythin'!

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.880
Like how to get chicks!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.380
No, I'm not good with girls...

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.840
Wait, so do you lean the other way?

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.340
Is that why you joined the team?!

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.880
No.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:42.880
Coach Takagi said we're going to rewatch
the school festival routine later today.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:43.550
What?

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.420
She messaged us.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.320
Coach Takagi

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.320
Today we'll review the school festival
 routine. I recorded it. Come prepared!

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.840
With hearts and everything!

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:05.630
That's an OG, all right...

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.050
Oh Gee?

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.460
Short for One Giant Forehead.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.340
--Ow!
--Did you say something?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.800
We didn't say nuthin'!

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.630
One Giant Forehead...

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:18.710
So this is the level you're at...

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:21.710
It's nothing compared to Dreams,

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.460
let alone Sparks.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:29.510
Yes, you're completely out of their league.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:35.170
However, it's clear that you thought like
amateurs and practiced as hard as you could.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:39.170
Of course, when it comes to technique,
you're far behind Dreams.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:43.010
But anyone can master the
techniques with practice.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.760
To put it another way,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.550
the Breakers could surpass
Dreams very soon!

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.880
I want to see all of you...

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.300
...standing on this stage!

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:01.090
National

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:01.710
Cheerleading

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:02.710
Championship

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:05.100
National Cheerleading Championship

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.920
The National Championship!

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.260
It'll take place in Makuhari
at the end of March.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:16.300
Dreams competes every year,
and they've placed in the top 3.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:21.380
But if your routine doesn't score enough points
during the qualifiers at the end of January,

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.800
then you can't participate.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.130
January...

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.340
That's only about 3 months from now.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.050
We'll never be able to get enough
points with so little time.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.380
'Course we can do it!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.710
Saku...

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:40.630
The routine from the school festival
was so cool! So we'll be just fine.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:44.670
Mori, why're you saying we're
doomed before we've even tried?

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.130
Right on!

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.460
Let's give it a shot and pass the qualifiers!

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.210
Yes, let's!

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.210
I'll be right behind ya.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.550
So will we!

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:53.840
We'll do our best, too!

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:55.380
Right, Bro!

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.380
Whatever, let's stand out from the crowd!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:00.130
Coach, we'll be counting on you!

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.210
Anyway, if you're going to
compete in the championship,

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:08.340
I require all of you to improve your skills.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.210
Kazu.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.460
Whoa! First-name basis already!

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.210
You're the captain, right?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.010
Yes!

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.300
Then, Sho...

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.130
You'll be the drill captain.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:22.210
You're in charge of training the new members.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.420
Right.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:34.460
So fried pork curry with noodles and
rice consists of three different things...

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.880
Say, why're you followin' us around?

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.510
I'm learnin' everyday Japanese!

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.460
It's so spicy!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.550
Here.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:48.170
Captain Hashimoto, you're so nice!

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:50.130
You can call me Kazu.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.510
Kazu...

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:55.090
You're like one of those girls.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.760
You don't call 'em that these days.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.800
The National Championship...

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.630
All of a sudden the bar
just got raised way higher.

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:06.920
Coach Takagi says she'll supervise us
twice a week on Tuesdays and Fridays.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:09.800
On those days we'll have
to take over the gym.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:13.630
On Mondays and Wednesdays
we'll practice on Haru's roof.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:14.760
Got it.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:18.300
Some guys have jobs on the weekend,
so let's practice on our own those days.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.550
We'll only have Thursday off!

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:26.840
"Dream as if you'll live forever.
Live as if you'll die today."

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.130
Dixit James Dean.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.880
Those are the perfect words
to describe us right now.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:36.170
We need to practice as if everything
begins and ends today.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:40.170
Yeah. And since we have more members,
we'll have to push ourselves hard.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.380
Right, let's finish up and head out!

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.760
Okay!

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:49.550
What's wrong?

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:57.380
I think we'll head back this way today!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.590
But why?

00:11:58.590 --> 00:11:59.800
What's going on?

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.210
That's the long way to the train station!

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:05.010
Gotta walk off that meal!

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.050
What in the...?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.550
Eh, whatever.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.130
Bandou Gym

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.960
The shower's free now.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.420
'Kay.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.340
Whoa, it's the Great Square of Pegasus.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:31.340
Say, Kazu...

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.420
Hm?

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.300
You're always worrying
about me, aren't you?

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.960
I hadn't realized it...

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:43.010
You made sure we wouldn't be around when
the guys from Judo Club came to the caf.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.760
That place is pretty small, y'know.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:50.010
With them around there'd be no seats left.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.960
How pathetic.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.010
You keep having to look out for me.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:57.630
Because you stuck with me.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.920
Back when I said I wanted to do cheerleading.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:06.340
Let's make it to the National Championship.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.960
If we do, then the judo guys...

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:12.340
...and even Haruko will accept us.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.550
Sure.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.670
First we'll work on strengthening your core!

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.800
Be a man and suck it up!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.420
Grin and bear it!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.550
B-But...!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.960
We will, Big Bro!

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.840
There's no need to push
yourselves so hard.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:54.090
Work on maintaining good posture, and you'll
eventually learn to keep it as you train.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:56.630
Thank you very much, sir!

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.210
You okay?

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.340
Yeah...

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.510
So you're... Ando?

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:07.880
Takeru's fine!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.840
You could get someone hurt,
so stop horsing around.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.880
Bro! Don't wear my shirt!

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.260
What's yours is mine!

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.380
Huh?

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.340
I've heard that line a lot.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.380
So you have a big brother, too, Bando!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.050
No, a sister.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.710
Sister?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.510
He's trying so hard to help them.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.630
Kinda feels like he's changed!

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:33.510
Haru's the defender of the newbies.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:37.510
Yeah, he's a real mother hen.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.300
He's always been this way.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:45.630
Thank you very much!

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:48.880
Wait, I have something to give you all.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:50.880
What's this?

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.920
A notebook for recording your thoughts.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:57.760
Every day after practice ends,
write down anything that comes to mind.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.510
Why're we doing this?

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:02.550
To face yourselves.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:08.130
This is the best thing to do when you're
pursuing a goal with your sights set high.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.090
I've written the first page for you.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.210
Everyone has a different topic.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:26.980
<b>BEAT KAZU!</b>

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:32.460
What is it?

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.170
Um... About this...

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.760
Haru.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.510
You're terrible compared to Kazu.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:45.050
Your flexibility, your center of balance...
Kazu is one step ahead of you on everything.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:50.800
And yet, you don't think of him as a rival.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.170
I'm sure you already know this.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:57.670
You will not advance until you surpass Kazu.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:00.210
By the way, Sho!

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:03.760
Decide on everyone's positions by Friday.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.010
All right.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.300
Coach, please allow me to escort you home.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.460
I'll be fine.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:14.550
So, what'd she write in your notebook?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.420
Sho?

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:19.960
Oh, sorry. To think about the positions...

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.420
Come on in!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:23.010
I'll do it.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.550
May I have your order?

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.630
I...

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:30.260
I'll have a cappuccino!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.380
Flyers: Kazu, Haru, Saku.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:39.210
Bases: Ton, Ichiro, Hisashi,
Takuya, Takumi, Kin, Takeru.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:42.300
Spotters: Mizoguchi, Gen, Gin, Doh.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:46.380
14 in all. We're missing someone.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:50.460
Oh, I know, Bro! The guy who wrote it!

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.340
How long do you plan on running?

00:16:57.340 --> 00:17:01.550
You were a first-class base,
and a pillar of the team.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.420
Make no mistake.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.300
Sho!

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.550
I'm sorry for running off like that.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.920
Wanna go grab something to eat?

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:43.260
I'm making everyone worry about me.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:45.380
And nobody asks a thing...

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:48.800
Everybody's got things they
don't want to talk about.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.340
That's what Kazu said.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:55.090
I'm probably making everyone worry, too.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:18:01.130
My family runs a dojo, and yet nobody
has asked me why I quit judo.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.630
It's true I hurt my shoulder, but...

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:06.670
I just couldn't win.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:11.300
My sister's so strong, she won
the national championship.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:14.090
I, on the other hand...

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.760
I was a student at Yomei High School.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:20.880
Then...

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.300
You were a base on Yomei's team, Sparks?

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:31.880
Coach Takagi was teaching us back then.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:36.300
In the summer of my third year,
we competed in the last Summer Cup.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:41.880
We tried to make the best 2 minute
30 second routine in Japan.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:45.840
But in the finals...

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:50.670
I dropped her... Sakura.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.340
Who's Sakura?

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:03.170
The coach's little sister.

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:08.420
Sakura was our team's ace,
full of life and light,

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:11.880
the teammate who supported everyone...

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.050
But...

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:24.050
Sakura... injured her back.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.710
It's fine, I'll get better.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.550
I'm going to keep doing cheerleading.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:34.050
And you'll keep doing it, too, right Sho?

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:39.880
When you're my base, I can fly
without a care in the world.

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.670
But I'm afraid.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:49.090
Afraid that if I'm the base,
I'll drop someone again.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:54.630
Just like the coach said,
I'm running away.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:20:00.130
I know that... and yet, I...

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.050
Sho!

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:02.460
Sorry.

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.800
I'm done for today.

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:15.170
Yeah, I'll work hard! We'll
definitely win the next one, too!

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.710
I'm running away, too.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.320
<b>BEAT KAZU!</b>

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.300
But...

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:31.130
Let me tell our coach about the positions.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:34.380
Just like before, it's fine
if you don't do any stunts.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:37.840
That's right! I don't know your reason
for it, but don't force yourself!

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:41.630
You've been whippin' the
newbies into good shape!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.670
And us, too, of course.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.090
Oh, Hashimoto! Long time no see!

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:52.260
Nice hustle.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:55.300
Oh? Bando, too!

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:58.380
You guys are doing
men's cheerleading, right?

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.300
I saw your debut!

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.920
Go, fight, win!

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:06.550
What the hell?

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:09.550
We are.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:13.340
We're doing all-men's cheerleading.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:16.510
We're competing in a tournament soon.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:19.130
So that we can make it to
the National Championship.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.380
O-Oh, really?

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.670
Well, let's both do our best!

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.010
See ya!

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.260
Haru...

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:32.260
I can't run away.

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:35.170
I have to face myself.

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.300
And probably, Sho does, too.

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:40.920
In judo, you throw your opponent, right?

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:43.760
But everyone learns how to fall
when they're thrown, too.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.710
So even if you get thrown
real fast, you're okay.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:49.840
I was really good at receiving throws.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.050
Kazu, too!

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.090
There! Wasn't that good?

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:01.800
W-What are you saying?

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.960
Uh, I mean...

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.010
So you don't have to be scared...

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:08.170
Judo and cheerleading are
two different things!

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:09.130
That's right!

00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:10.260
No, Haru's saying--

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:13.340
Believe. That's what he's saying.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:38.460
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:45.050
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:48.460
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:51.840
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:55.130
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:55.130 --> 00:23:01.710
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:04.630
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:07.920
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:10.010
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:10.010 --> 00:23:11.670
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:16.170
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:19.590
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:23.300
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:26.630
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:29.920
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:36.550
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:39.710
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:43.090
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:51.210
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:57.420
Practice's only just started!

00:23:57.420 --> 00:23:58.800
Let's take it slow!

00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:00.340
Slow? Are you a turtle?

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:02.550
--Huh?
--No, that's an insult to turtles.

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:03.210
You're below a turtle.

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.050
You jerk!

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:09.920
Next Episode: Strain.

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:08.010
Next Episode: Strain.

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:09.920
Let's go, Breakers!
